{"item_id":"generic-02","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"none","category":"coherent_prose","subset":"generic_english","text":"Mara found the missing envelope beneath a stack of old magazines. She put it beside the front door so she would remember to carry it with her the next morning."}
{"item_id":"generic-03","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"none","category":"coherent_prose","subset":"generic_english","text":"The neighborhood meeting began late because several chairs were still locked in a storage room. Once everyone had a seat, the group quickly agreed on a date for the autumn cleanup."}
{"item_id":"generic-04","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"none","category":"coherent_prose","subset":"generic_english","text":"A narrow footpath follows the river for several miles before turning toward the hills. On weekdays it is mostly used by commuters taking a shortcut between the station and the offices."}
{"item_id":"generic-05","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"none","category":"coherent_prose","subset":"generic_english","text":"Jon replaced the hallway bulb and noticed that the new light made the faded wallpaper look brighter. He left the ladder by the stairs until his neighbor returned to borrow it."}
{"item_id":"generic-06","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"none","category":"coherent_prose","subset":"generic_english","text":"The notice on the lobby board announced that the lift would be unavailable on Tuesday. Most residents read it in passing, but someone added a handwritten reminder near the mailboxes."}
{"item_id":"generic-07","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"none","category":"coherent_prose","subset":"generic_english","text":"After the rain stopped, the market square filled slowly with bicycles and umbrellas. Vendors reopened their stalls while a delivery van waited for enough space to turn around."}
{"item_id":"generic-08","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"none","category":"coherent_prose","subset":"generic_english","text":"The office moved its weekly meeting from Thursday to Friday without changing the agenda. An updated invitation reached everyone before lunch, so the room booking was the only detail left to fix."}
{"item_id":"generic-09","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"none","category":"coherent_prose","subset":"generic_english","text":"A cardboard box arrived with one corner bent, although everything inside was undamaged. Leila kept the packing paper for a future move and placed the empty box beside the recycling bin."}
{"item_id":"generic-10","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"none","category":"coherent_prose","subset":"generic_english","text":"The local bus now pauses at the temporary stop across from the old cinema. A small sign gives the new timetable, and regular passengers have already adjusted their usual route."}
{"item_id":"verse-01","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"poetry","category":"verse_fragment","subset":"verse","text":"At dusk the patient windows gleam,\nthen fade like lanterns in a dream;\nthe street grows still beneath the rain."}
{"item_id":"verse-02","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"poetry","category":"verse_fragment","subset":"verse","text":"O little moon above the wire,\nyou silver every rooftop spire\nand wake the shadows one by one."}
{"item_id":"verse-03","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"poetry","category":"verse_fragment","subset":"verse","text":"The wind has borrowed autumn's coat;\nit trails red leaves beside the moat,\nthen leaves them sleeping at the gate."}
{"item_id":"verse-04","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"poetry","category":"verse_fragment","subset":"verse","text":"Between two bells the silence stays,\na quiet room of folded days,\nwhere dust turns slowly in the sun."}
{"item_id":"verse-05","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"poetry","category":"verse_fragment","subset":"verse","text":"River, carry my name downstream,\npast willow root and broken beam;\nreturn with only stars to keep."}
{"item_id":"verse-06","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"poetry","category":"verse_fragment","subset":"verse","text":"The sparrow writes upon the snow\na script the morning cannot know;\nby noon, each fragile mark is gone."}
{"item_id":"verse-07","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"poetry","category":"verse_fragment","subset":"verse","text":"Night gathers blue along the shore,\nand every wave repeats once more\nthe word the daylight would not say."}
{"item_id":"verse-08","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"poetry","category":"verse_fragment","subset":"verse","text":"Old clock, be gentle with the hour;\ndo not disturb the sleeping flower\nthat closes when the daylight ends."}
{"item_id":"verse-09","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"poetry","category":"verse_fragment","subset":"verse","text":"A single cloud, a field of wheat,\nthe summer humming at my feet,\nand far away a closing door."}
{"item_id":"verse-10","arm":"calibration","seed":0,"step":-1,"layer":-1,"snippet_set":"judge-calibration-round2","modality":"text","expected_label":"poetry","category":"verse_fragment","subset":"verse","text":"When morning lifts its amber wing,\nthe chimneys wake, the cables sing,\nand footsteps bloom along the square."}
